// @check
// @error wrong number of arguments: expected 1 to 2, got 0
// A default widens the accepted arity to a RANGE, and the diagnostic names the
// range rather than a single number — so a caller that supplies too few (or too
// many) arguments is told which calls are legal, not only which one is not.
function k(a: i32, b: i32 = 2): i32 { a + b }
print(k())
